After work I come home.
In the hallway I meet Sabine and her dog Bruno.
Bruno is a small and sweet dog.
He barks loudly, for he is happy.
"Hello Maya," says Sabine.
"You are freezing."
That is true.
I am only wearing a thin jacket today.
"I finally need a thick winter coat," I say.
"Do you have a good tip, Sabine?"
Sabine thinks for a moment.
"You will find a large shop in the city centre," she answers.
"The shop sells very good winter clothes."
"And they have a large selection," says Sabine.
"Is the warm clothing very expensive?" I ask.
"No, it is not expensive, but the quality is great," says Sabine.
That is a great tip.
I thank Sabine for the help.
On Saturday I will visit the large shop.
